# CodeCraftHub 🚀

CodeCraftHub is a lightweight, beginner-friendly RESTful API built with Python and Flask. It allows you to create, view, update, and delete courses to help track your learning progress. All data is persisted locally in a simple JSON file—no complex database configuration required!

This project is designed as a learning tool for understanding REST API fundamentals, HTTP methods, JSON payloads, and basic server-side validation.

---

## ✨ Features

- **Full CRUD Support:** Create, Read, Update, and Delete course entries.
- **Data Persistence:** Automatically stores and reads course records from `courses.json`.
- **Input Validation:** Enforces required fields, date formats (`YYYY-MM-DD`), and allowed status values.
- **Robust Error Handling:** Returns standard HTTP status codes (`200`, `201`, `400`, `404`, `405`, `500`) with readable JSON error messages.
- **Zero Database Setup:** Starts working right out of the box using standard Python libraries.

---

## 📁 Project Structure

```text
CodeCraftHub/
│
├── venv/                 # Isolated Python virtual environment (ignored by Git)
├── app.py                # Main Flask application and REST API endpoints
├── courses.json          # Local JSON file where course data is saved
├── requirements.txt      # List of Python package dependencies (Flask)
└── README.md             # Project documentation and guide